    });
  }

  /**
   * A designed quantity stepper over a real <input type="number">.
   *
   * WHY THE INPUT IS REAL AND NOT A <span>. WooCommerce reads the quantity
   * straight out of the request, so on a GET add-to-cart form the value has to
   * live in a NAMED form control or the cart receives nothing and silently
   * adds one. Keeping a native number input also means the control still works
   * with this runtime absent — the browser's own spinner does the job — which
   * matters because a section can be exported to a page where the js never
   * runs. The buttons are progressive enhancement over a working control, not
   * the control itself.
   *
